    "lawCode": "Amd §378, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2791\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the executive law and the general business law, in\nrelation to establishing Amanda's law requiring all owners of\nresidences with appliances, devices or systems emitting carbon\nmonoxide to purchase and install carbon monoxide detectors when such\nappliance, device or system is replaced\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo mandate whenever an appliance that emits carbon monoxide is\nreplaced or installed that a carbon monoxide detector is installed.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection I:  establishes \"Amanda's Law\"\n\nSection II: creates a new subdivision of section 378 of the executive\nlaw regarding standards for the installation of carbon monoxide\ndetectors in all residences having appliances, devices or systems\nwhich emit carbon monoxide. Any contractor or any other person\nreplacing an appliance, device or system which emits carbon monoxide\nmust install a carbon monoxide detector if one is not already present\nin such residence, at the same time. Any violation of this section\nshall be punishable by a civic penalty not to exceed one hundred\ndollars.\n\nSection III: requires a posting of notice when appliances, devices or\nsystems which emit carbon monoxide are sold. The posting must be in\nlegible format and in close proximity to any appliances, devices or\nsystems displayed for sale, the posting must read: \"The New York State\nExecutive law requires owners of residences to purchase and install\ncarbon monoxide detectors if one is not already present, when\nreplacing an appliance, device or system which emits carbon monoxide.\"\n\nSection IV: effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nOn January 17, 2009 Amanda Hansen, a 16 year old from West Seneca, New\nYork, died from carbon monoxide poisoning from a defective boiler\nwhile at a sleepover at her friend's house.  This first part of this\nlegislation requires anybody who is replacing any appliance that emits\ncarbon monoxide to also install a carbon monoxide detector. By\nrequiring this, we will ensure that New Yorker's take precautions\nagainst this deadly silent killer.  This legislation is also aimed at\npromoting awareness by requiring retailers to post for consumers the\ndangers of carbon monoxide, and encourage them before tragedies\nhappen.  This legislation would prevent tragic accidents like Amanda's\nfrom happening in the future.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become law.\n",
